# Suite-wide rules, from coffee-pub-blacksmith/.gitattributes. ADDED to this file, never
# copied over it -- see the packs rule at the bottom, which the hub does not carry and
# which a wholesale copy would have silently removed.

# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# JavaScript files
*.js text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.cjs text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf

# Web files
*.html text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.hbs text eol=lf

# Documentation
*.md text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf

# The files every module copies from the hub unchanged. Without these, `text=auto` plus
# core.autocrlf=true turns them CRLF in the working tree on the next checkout while the hub's stay LF,
# and a byte-identity diff then reports every line changed -- looking exactly like a local edit.
# .yml and the two dotfiles are the three of the five copied files that no extension rule reaches.
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
.gitignore text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf

# Images should be treated as binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.svg text eol=lf

# Font files
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ARTIFICER-SPECIFIC, AND IT MUST STAY LAST.
#
# LevelDB pack files: treat as binary so line endings are not converted (Foundry v11
# packaging guide). Prevents "cannot connect to database" errors when developing on Windows.
#
# THE POSITION IS LOAD-BEARING. Git applies the LAST matching rule, so this has to come
# after `* text=auto` above or that rule wins and eight compendiums get line-ending
# conversion run over them -- silently, on checkout, with the damage already in the working
# tree. Most files inside a pack (`LOG`, `CURRENT`, `MANIFEST-000123`) have no extension, so
# no other rule here reaches them; `*` is the only thing that would, and this is what stops it.
packs/** binary
